{
  "id": "sockets",
  "title": "Socket controllers",
  "summary": "SocketRoute marks a controller class that keeps a WebSocket open, as Jakarta's @ServerEndpoint does. Tachyon makes one object of the class for each connection, so its fields hold that connection's state. OnOpen, OnMessage, OnClose and OnError mark the methods that run when a browser connects, sends a message, leaves, or when a method fails. Each message is JSON text, and Tachyon checks it against the model type of the OnMessage parameter first. The session sends messages back, and openSessions() (open_sessions() in Python, Ruby and Rust, OpenSessions() in Go, C# and F#, getOpenSessions() in Java) returns every open connection of the same path, so one message can go to every tab. When OnOpen or OnMessage fails, OnError runs and the socket stays open, as in Jakarta. In the browser, SocketRequest on an HTTPClient method receives the messages and publishes each one as its model's event, and the client's send(message) writes to the socket. Sockets are written in any Yon language. `Public`, `SignedIn` or `Allow(Role)` on the class says who may connect; Tachyon answers 401 or 403 before it opens the socket.",
  "group": "Yon server",
